WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:08.620
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, for my first
Arrow winter break video I wanted to get into

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:14.530
some of the stuff we know about the back half
of the season.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.750
We already know the general arc of The Black
Canary.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.810
Some people are calling the next three episodes
the Canary Trilogy.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.080
And Oliver has this really big Flashback storyline.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.080
Which will feature Amanda Waller a lot more
prominently.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.550
And yes, even though the DC movies and the
tv shows are officially separate universes.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:33.830
I do think the Suicide Squad movie happening
so soon is going to have some influence on

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.330
the way the show can use those characters.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.900
I’ll explain what I mean.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.470
Let’s do Oliver first, because I know that’s
what everyone is going crazy about.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:46.980
He is very clearly at the point of death,
so just as a way to side step his recovery

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.270
be it through use of Lazarus Pit or more traditional
means.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.800
Stephen Amell can’t just totally check out
of the show for 4 or 5 episodes.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.809
That’s where the flashbacks come in.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:59.760
He’s been posting a crazy number of pictures
to Social Media that feature him with the

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.309
classic Flashback wig on.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:03.710
But there was also this one of him with Robbie
Amell.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.470
I don’t think Firestorm is going to go back
in time or anything.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.880
I just think that Robbie Amell was visiting
the set.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:10.880
Not to shoot any Firestorm scenes.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.250
Arrow and The Flash share a production budget
and they also film on adjacent studio lots.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.929
So the actors can walk over if and say hi
to each other if they have enough time.

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:21.100
As of Episode 9 all we know about Hong Kong
is that Maseo’s wife, Katana and their son

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.640
have been kidnapped by China White.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.140
And she has a bioweapon.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:33.780
So the real goal of the flashbacks for the
rest of the season are fixing those two problems.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.760
Because of the way Maseo was acting in present
day.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.400
It seemed like his wife and son died and he
wanted to leave his old life behind.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:49.070
That’s why I think he said Maseo no longer
exists when Oliver first recognized him.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:57.360
That doesn’t guarantee they die in the flashbacks,
but if they’re doing a version of Katana’s

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.860
origin story from the comics, then they have
to.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.830
It’s just in Arrow’s version of events.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.110
Maseo seems like he’s taken on the Katana
persona.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:09.950
These are the titles of the next four episodes
and all the info we have on them.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:16.500
But something really important to remember
is that Stephen Amell said in the back half

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.200
of the season, just like season 2, every four
episodes or so is it’s own self contained

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.340
storyline.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.690
So there will be at least two or three big
arcs.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:38.020
10 is 

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:49.489
called Left Behind, 11 is called Midnight
City, 12 is Uprising, 13 is Canaries and 14

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:52.580
is The Return.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:03:00.900
I’m mostly going to focus on what the producers
have said about the Flashback storylines and

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:07.190
the Black Canary and where I think those things
are headed.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:12.410
The titles of the episodes usually reflect
things happening in present day and in the

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.410
flashbacks.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.740
Left Behind is mostly a reference to Team
Arrow.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.530
All the people Oliver leaves behind.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.940
There’s this big christian novel series
about what happens to the survivors after

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:27.050
most of the world’s population gets raptured.

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:33.691
So if we do see Hong Kong scenes in this episode
I think they will be minimal.

00:03:33.691 --> 00:03:35.690
But they do have to follow up on the big WTF
with China White taking Maseo’s family and

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:36.690
the bioweapon.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.880
So they’ll tee up Amanda Waller’s plan
for cleaning up that mess.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.990
But really I think the focus will be on the
surviving members of Team Arrow and how they

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:42.990
learn to continue Oliver’s mission when
he’s not around.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.990
I’m really interested to see if Nyssa tells
them Oliver is dead.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.990
She’s their only point of contact with the
League of Assassins.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:45.990
So if they find out what happened right away.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:46.990
It’s either from Nyssa or Merlyn.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.170
I think Oliver not being around will create
a bit of a vacuum and crime will get a little

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.170
worse.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.330
And that will kick Laurel into putting on
the Black Canary costume.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.200
Like the way crime rates in Gotham double
when Batman isn’t around for an extended

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.200
period of time.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.700
She will get the costume during the episode.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:04.140
But because it’s a huge deal I think they’ll
save it for like a big third act reveal.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.190
Another Batman Begins type thing.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:09.150
Batman goes out without the cowl and no one
is afraid of him.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.720
Laurel comes back at the end of the episode.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:16.870
Puts the costume on and starts trying to scare
the shit out of people.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:21.260
Then the next two or three episodes after
that is her Batman Year One story.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.950
She gets her ass handed too her until she
gets her shit together to the point where

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:31.770
she can actually catch criminals without breaking
every bone in her body.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:36.570
Stephen Amell was really clear that Laurel
wouldn’t just put the costume on and automatically

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.570
be Black Canary.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:45.600
It’s going to be just like Roy.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.020
It took him an entire season to figure it
out and Nyssa still beat the shit out of him

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.240
without breaking a sweat.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.540
So even Roy still has a long way to go.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:59.400
I’m really interested to see if Laurel compels
Wildcat to come back into action to help them

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.400
out.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:10.620
It seems like it would be unfair for them
to tease that in the Boxing Glove episode

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.960
and not give us our Justice Society moment.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:30.900
Midnight City Episode 11 could be a reference
to Doctor Mid Nite.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:35.910
The writer who wrote this episode is the one
who also brought Doctor Mid Nite back in the

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.460
Green Arrow comics.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:43.770
He was a member of the Justice Society.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.340
I know I keep saying Justice Society on Arrow.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:50.620
And I really think we’ll get there by the
end of the season.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.190
Not in the traditional sense like they call
themselves Justice Society.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.750
We’ll just get enough of those characters
on the show working together that it seems

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.910
like Justice Society.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:06.250
Episode 12 Uprising could be the start of
Diggle and Lyla taking control of Argus.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.889
Sin is returning too.

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:10.780
In know everyone wanted her to come back.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:16.460
It seems like she’ll have been living in
the Glades this whole time.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:26.550
I hope they explain why she lost touch with
Roy.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.850
The actors said that they would being effectively
taking control of Argus from amanda waller

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.060
this season.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:33.910
They didn’t say why, only that Waller would
have other priorities.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:39.300
It could be a side effect of the Suicide Squad
movie, but they might also use it as an opportunity

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:45.200
for Amanda Waller to found a new team like
the Outsiders or some other team up they’ll

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.300
prep for season 4.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:53.560
It’s also worth noting that Vinny Jones
will be in both Episode 11 and 12 as Brick

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.560
from the comics.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.120
His name, Danny Brickwell also appeared on
Oliver’s List from Season 1.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.640
Episode 13 Canaries is a big flashback episode.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:13.320
It will tell the story of how Sara joined
the League of Assassins.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:17.699
Maseo said that he joined at the same time
as Sara, so he’ll probably be in those episodes

00:07:17.699 --> 00:07:18.699
too.

00:07:18.699 --> 00:07:19.699
Caity Lotz is coming back.

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:20.730
She’ll be alive because everything is happening
in the past.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.330
Episode 14 is the Slade Episode.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:28.960
Manu Bennett came back but we don’t know
if it’s in present day or in a flashback.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.360
And Marc Guggenhein was very specific that
the title “The Return” doesn’t refer

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.690
to Oliver’s return or Slade’s Return.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.340
So take from that what you will.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:40.400
Someone or something else is returning.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:47.320
In that episode Marc Singer of Beastmaster
fame will be playing Matthew Shrieve from

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.320
the comics.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:52.730
But he is confirmed as a flashback character.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.210
In the comics he’s the head of the Creature
Commandos.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.960
A US military team of supernatural creatures.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.460
Shrieve is the only human on the team.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.740
It’s supposed to be a big arc.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.340
So we could see a flashback metahuman team.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.639
In the new 52 comics they’re a SHADE team.

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:10.660
But it’s still the same deal, superhuman
military task force led by Frankenstein.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.699
I’m not expecting to see frankenstein on
the tv show though.

00:08:13.699 --> 00:08:15.020
But look out for easter eggs.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:19.759
Episode 15 is called Nanda Parbat.

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:26.539
I’m hoping we get to see Oliver in Nanda
Parbat in present day.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:30.389
But we could see team arrow member road trip
out there to try and bring him back.

00:08:30.389 --> 00:08:33.829
Those are all the episodes we know about right
now.

00:08:33.829 --> 00:08:35.339
That still leaves 7.

00:08:35.339 --> 00:08:41.419
So there’s so much more that’s going to
happen.

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:47.379
Yes I do think Ray Palmer will fight with
Team Arrow, yes I do think Oliver will be

00:08:47.379 --> 00:08:55.329
back in Starling in present day before the
last couple 

00:08:55.329 --> 00:08:56.329
of episodes.

00:08:56.329 --> 00:08:58.790
Yes Merlyn will team up with Oliver at some
point.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.319
And only for a very brief period.

00:09:02.319 --> 00:09:04.990
Oliver still hates him.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:10.249
And as for the DJ in the nightclub.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:14.139
I don’t think he’s Joe, Deathstroke’s
son.

00:09:14.139 --> 00:09:30.939
But I do think he’ll end up being a bigger
part of 

00:09:30.939 --> 00:09:36.910
the narrative.

